{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 TR-909 style drum machine: circuit-modelled kick, snare, toms, rim shot and hand clap, sampled hi-hats, ride and crash, per-voice drive, distortion, pan and reverb/delay sends, master distortion and glue compressor, stereo or 11-channel multi-out (one output per voice as on the TR-909's back panel, hi-hats shared, plus an FX return; pan, master distortion and compressor are stereo only), ported from 9W9 by athousanddetails, after ER-99 by Matthew Cieplak https://github.com/athousanddetails/schwung-9W9 (GPLv3) JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license Claude generated some of this code\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 String ensemble playing S. Christian Collins' SCC Expressive Strings through a port of the sfizz SFZ engine. Seven key-switched articulations: legato with expression control, legato with velocity control, staccato, pizzicato, tremolo (expression or velocity) and a legato/tremolo crossfade on the soft pedal (CC67). Expression on the mod wheel (CC1), breath (CC2), foot (CC4) or expression (CC11). Ported from sfizz 1.2.3 (sfizz authors, https://sfz.tools/sfizz, BSD 2-clause). Instrument: SCC Expressive Strings 1.0 by S. Christian Collins (https://www.schristiancollins.com), released as "use at your own risk"; samples collected by the author from free SoundFont banks (Dependencies/EvangelinaSymphonica/Espressivo-LICENSE.txt). JSFX code released under GPLv3+ license Claude generated some of this code\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Acoustic drum kit based on the AVL Drumkits Blonde Bop, played with sticks or Hot Rods (from Blonde Bop HR), 27 pieces on the GM drum map (notes 35-61, stick click on 35), 135 samples per set with five velocity layers, hi-hat and cymbal chokes, clickable kit photo, stereo or multi-channel (kick, snare, hi-hat, tom, floor tom, overheads, percussion) outputs, ported from avldrums.lv2 by Robin Gareus (fluidsynth sample engine, kit photo and hit map) https://github.com/x42/avldrums.lv2 (GPLv2+) Samples and kit photo: AVL Drumkits (Blonde Bop) by Glen MacArthur, http://www.bandshed.net/avldrumkits/ Samples as modified for avldrums.lv2, then reduced to 12-bit and joined into one file per set for this plugin; the sample files remain under CC-BY-SA 3.0 (see Dependencies/Drumkits/Goldibops-LICENSE.txt), and music made with it can be licensed freely JSFX code released under GPLv3+ license Claude Opus 5.x may have generated some of the port of this code\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A port of Mutable Instruments Grids, the topographic drum sequencer. Map X and Map Y move around a 5 x 5 map of drum patterns, blending between the nearest four. The three Fill knobs set how busy each part is, and Chaos shakes the pattern a little more each time round. Euclidean mode swaps the map for three euclidean rhythms: the X, Y and Chaos knobs set each part's length, the Fill knobs its number of hits. Grids makes MIDI only, so put a drum instrument after it on the same track (Dr Nine, Captain's Kit, or any drum sampler). It follows REAPER's transport, or runs free at its own tempo, and locks to the bar. Accented hits play at the Accent velocity. The module's three extra outputs (accents, or clock and bar) can go out as extra notes through the Aux selector. Ported from Grids by Emilie Gillet (Mutable Instruments) https://github.com/pichenettes/eurorack (GPLv3+) JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license Claude generated some of this code\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A modal synthesizer in the style of Mutable Instruments Elements: a bowed, blown and struck exciter feeding a 64-mode resonator (or a string, or five strings tuned to a chord), followed by the module's stereo spread and reverb. Ominous Voice is the module's hidden FM drone voice. Play it from MIDI: velocity sets the strength (accent), channel pressure changes it while a note is held, the mod wheel drives pitch through the FM knob, and pitch bend has its own range. Audio on the left input excites the strike path, the right input the blow path. Needs Dependencies/InYourElement/elements_tables.txt. Ported from Elements by Emilie Gillet (Mutable Instruments) https://github.com/pichenettes/eurorack (MIT) JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license Claude generated some of this code\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Two-oscillator subtractive polysynth with LFO, filter, distortion and reverb, ported from amsynth by Nick Dowell https://github.com/amsynth/amsynth (GPLv2+) Reverb: Freeverb by Jezar at Dreampoint (public domain) Bundled presets: the 28 banks shipped with amsynth (Factory, BriansBank01-22, PatriksBank01-05) User bank of 128 slots: STORE the current sound from any bank, INIT, rename; saved with the project and in REAPER presets JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license Claude generated some of this code\par}
}

