{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Make a synth talk. TalkBox mode models your voice with LPC (like a talk box tube in your mouth), Vocoder mode is a classic 8 or 16 band channel vocoder with five presets. By default the voice is the track's own audio (channels 1+2) and the synth comes in on the sidechain (channels 3+4): send a synth track to this track's channels 3/4. You can also feed a stereo signal with the voice on one side and the synth on the other. Bright, buzzy synths (saws, squares, pads) work best as the carrier. Ported from mda TalkBox and mda Vocoder by Paul Kellett (Maxim Digital Audio), via mda-effects https://github.com/pluginguru/mda-effects (MIT or GPLv2+) JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license Claude generated some of this code\par}
}

