{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A port of Mutable Instruments Marbles, the random sampler. Three gate streams (t1, t2, t3) make rhythms and three random pitch streams (X1, X2, X3) make melodies. Y is a slower random value sent as a MIDI CC. Deja Vu is the heart of it: below 12 o'clock the randomness starts to repeat, at 12 o'clock it locks into a loop of the set Length, and above that it scrambles the loop. T and X each have their own Deja Vu button. Marbles makes MIDI only, so put an instrument after it on the same track. In Pitch mode each gate plays its own X value through the chosen scale; in Drums mode each gate plays a fixed note. It follows REAPER's transport, where Rate picks a multiple of the beat, or runs free at its own rate. Steps below 12 o'clock glides; above it quantizes to the scale, keeping fewer of the notes as it turns up. Needs Dependencies/LosingMyMarbles/marbles_tables.txt. Ported from Marbles by Emilie Gillet (Mutable Instruments) https://github.com/pichenettes/eurorack (MIT) JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license Claude generated some of this code\par}
}

