{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Additive and modulation synthesizer, a port of the ADsynth engine of ZynAddSubFX by Nasca Octavian Paul, Mark McCurry and the ZynAddSubFX contributors https://github.com/zynaddsubfx/zynaddsubfx (GPLv2+) Eight voices per note, each with its own harmonic oscillator (base functions, waveshaping, harmonic filters, spectral modulation and adjustment, adaptive harmonics), a modulator (morph, ring, phase, frequency or pulse-width modulation and oscillator sync), unison, noise sources, and amplitude, frequency and filter envelopes and LFOs. Analog, formant, state-variable, Moog and comb filters, resonance, punch, portamento, poly, mono and legato modes, and the ZynAddSubFX MIDI controller set. 19 factory patches built from the engine's own parameters, plus 122 instruments converted from the ZynAddSubFX banks (Dependencies/Partiality/Partiality-LICENSE.txt), in folders. Patches are saved with the project and in REAPER presets. JSFX code released under GPLv3+ license Claude generated some of this code\par}
}

