{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Sample quality reduction: lower the bit depth and sample rate, add harmonic "thickening", clip the peaks and muffle the result with a steep low-pass filter. Starts clean (24 bits, full rate, no thickening, filter off) so you can dial the damage in. Turn Rate left of centre to hold single samples (gritty, aliased) or right to hold averaged samples (smoother); turn Non-Lin left for even harmonics or right for odd harmonics. Mono sums the input like the original plugin; Stereo degrades each channel on its own. Ported from mda-lv2 by Paul Kellett (Maxim Digital Audio) and David Robillard https://gitlab.com/drobilla/mda-lv2 (GPLv3+) JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license Claude generated some of this code\par}
}

