{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 A granular texture processor in the style of Mutable Instruments Clouds. It records the incoming audio into a short buffer and plays it back as clouds of grains, as a pitch-shifted and time-stretched stream, as a looping delay, or through a spectral freeze-and-smear processor. Freeze holds the buffer so you can play with it. MIDI notes fire the trigger input (one grain, a tap tempo for the looping delay, a restart for the stretcher, a glitch in spectral mode) and can also transpose. Blend, spread, feedback and reverb sit behind the blend knob, as on the module. The engine runs at the module's 32 kHz with resampling to and from the project rate. Ported from Clouds by Emilie Gillet (Mutable Instruments) https://github.com/pichenettes/eurorack (MIT) JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license Claude generated some of this code\par}
}

