{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Spaghetti Junction MIDI Filters: a modular rack for the 34 x42 MIDI filters. Insert up to eight filters as blocks and patch them with cables from MIDI IN to MIDI OUT. An output can feed several inputs (parallel branches) and an input merges every cable plugged into it, so serial chains, key splits and layers are all possible. Right-click the canvas (or use ADD FILTER) to insert a filter after the selected block, or at the end of the chain when nothing is selected (hold Shift to insert it unpatched). Drag between an output jack and an input jack, in either direction, to add a cable; pull a cable well away from its path and release to unplug it. Right-click cables, jacks or blocks to disconnect, bypass, remove or reset. Delete removes the selected block. CABLE SLACK sets how loosely the cables hang. Notes still sounding are released whenever the patch changes. Requires REAPER 7 or later (more than 64 sliders). Ported from x42 midifilter.lv2 by Robin Gareus and contributors https://github.com/x42/midifilter.lv2 (GPLv2+) JSFX version released under GPLv3+ license Claude generated some of this code\par}
}

